{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#145","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#145","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#145\",\"parent_revision\":\"0e9fbb5df48d9da9b6daec18f6c5e468a89302a3f3c017bd2938cf22a677d70c\",\"root_revision\":\"0e9fbb5df48d9da9b6daec18f6c5e468a89302a3f3c017bd2938cf22a677d70c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Contradicting Evidence Unresolved\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#114 fixed PL006's data loss and kept its severity at `error`, on this reasoning: the \\\"unrecognized fields are warnings\\\" line comes from the **plugin.json** reference, not the marketplace one, and `tests/test_plugin_structure_validator.py` carries captured stderr showing the real marketplace validator emitting `Found 1 error: root: Unrecognized keys`.\\n\\nWhile implementing #114, the live `claude` CLI (v2.1.251, `.local/bin/claude`) was run against a `marketplace.json` carrying an unrecognized root key. **It returned a warning, not an error.**\\n\\nThat contradicts both the design brief's claim and the captured-stderr fixture the claim rests on. #114 said not to relitigate severity, so it was left at `error` and the observation was recorded rather than acted on \u2014 correctly, but it needs settling.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What To Determine\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Reproduce against the current `claude` CLI and record the exact invocation and output.\\n2. If the CLI warns, the captured stderr fixture in `test_plugin_structure_validator.py` is stale \u2014 find out which CLI version produced it and whether upstream changed the severity.\\n3. Then decide: match the platform, or keep `error` as a documented skilllint opinion with a `# Source: Lint opinion \u2014 \u2026` comment, the same way SK004/SK005 were resolved in #40.\\n\\nDowngrading on the wrong document's sentence would be an invented constraint. So would keeping `error` on a fixture that no longer reflects the tool.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #114 \u2014 where this was observed\\n- #40 \u2014 the \\\"lint opinion, not spec\\\" comment pattern\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3e983009af44315541e513a7e82c26ba79cdd772e4429c0d1585e1ff815f75f3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-RfQ\"}"}